## Run

    mise trust
    mise install
    mise run up

Each backend is an instance with its own origin, ports and database and, with identity, its own Kratos (with its own database) and session key. The backends share one Postgres server{{if .Run.PostgresService}}, `{{.Run.PostgresService}}` on host port {{.Run.PostgresPort}}{{end}}: every backend and every Kratos has its own database and user on it, created{{if .Run.PostgresInitService}} by `{{.Run.PostgresInitService}}`{{end}} on every `up`. Host ports {{.Run.PortLow}}-{{.Run.PortHigh}}, bound to `127.0.0.1`.

{{range .Instances}}- {{.Backend}}: {{.OriginURL}}{{if .Web}} (console {{.Web}}){{end}}; ports {{.Ports}}
{{end}}
Defaults are local-only placeholders. Per-instance overrides go in `.deploy/local/<component>/.env` (optional, keys as in the `.example.env` beside it). `.deploy/local/.env` is read only by compose interpolation and reaches every instance.
{{if .HasIdentity}}In Docker mode each Kratos takes its public origin from `APP_PUBLIC_BASE_URL_<COMPONENT>` in `.deploy/local/.env` (the component name in upper case, `-` as `_`; the default is the instance's origin above). To move an instance, set that variable and `APP_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` in the instance's `.env` to the same value.
{{end}}Without mise: `docker compose -f .deploy/local/docker-compose.yml --profile app up -d --build`.
Stop with `mise run down` (volumes kept). `.deploy/local/README.md` lists every port and service.
The compose project is `{{.Run.ComposeProject}}` (`<project name>-<port band>`). Two local stacks keep separate containers and volumes when their project name or port band differs; to run both at the same time their port bands must differ too. Projects with the same name and band share one compose project (containers, Postgres volume), and their host ports clash. Give each project its own name or port band.
{{if .CookieNote}}On `localhost` one browser profile is signed in to one identity instance at a time: signing in to the second overwrites the first's cookies. Use a second browser profile or a private window per instance.
{{end}}
## Edit a component on the host

Stop its container, then run it on the host on the same port (`mise run infra` starts the infrastructure alone). Per instance:
{{range .Instances}}
{{if .Web}}Editing {{.Web}}:

    docker compose -f .deploy/local/docker-compose.yml stop {{.Web}}
    mise run {{.DevWebTask}}

Editing {{.Backend}} runs {{.Web}} on the host too (nginx in the container reaches only the {{.Backend}} container); run each task in its own terminal:

    docker compose -f .deploy/local/docker-compose.yml stop {{.Backend}} {{.Web}}
    mise run {{.DevSrvTask}}
    mise run {{.DevWebTask}}

Once per clone: `npm --prefix {{.Web}} ci`.
{{else}}Editing {{.Backend}}:

    docker compose -f .deploy/local/docker-compose.yml stop {{.Backend}}
    mise run {{.DevSrvTask}}
{{end}}{{end}}
